== the permutation property: every cell exactly once, for every N
  ok: N = 1..300, 511, 512, 513, 1000, 4096, 5000; axes 0, 1, 7

== statelessness: point i does not depend on the other points
  ok: a point computed alone equals the point in the full design

== a value of an integer factor with range [10, 19] (ten levels) for N = 10 and N = 25
  N=10  points per level: {10: 1, 11: 1, 12: 1, 13: 1, 14: 1, 15: 1, 16: 1, 17: 1, 18: 1, 19: 1}
  N=25  points per level: {10: 2, 11: 3, 12: 2, 13: 3, 14: 2, 15: 3, 16: 2, 17: 3, 18: 2, 19: 3}

== 8 x 8 cells, N = 64 points in 2-D: empty cells (mean of 20 salts) against a stateless hash draw
  Latin hypercube  min 15  mean 20.0  max 25
  hash draw        min 20  mean 23.9  max 27
  (a hash draw leaves cells empty in expectation 64 * (63/64)^64 = 23.4)

== largest absolute correlation between two columns, d = 8, over 20 salts
   N   Latin hypercube (min mean max)   hash draw (min mean max)
   16   0.43 0.59 0.85                  0.37 0.53 0.75
   32   0.26 0.41 0.51                  0.30 0.41 0.61
   64   0.19 0.29 0.41                  0.18 0.27 0.39
  128   0.14 0.20 0.26                  0.13 0.20 0.26
  256   0.11 0.16 0.23                  0.09 0.14 0.18

== the exact stratification of every axis: sorted cells of axis 3, N = 12
  axis 3 cells by point: [1, 9, 6, 7, 5, 4, 0, 3, 10, 11, 2, 8]
  points 0..3 of N = 12 (cell of each axis):
   i=0  [10, 6, 0, 1]
   i=1  [8, 4, 3, 9]
   i=2  [6, 7, 10, 6]
   i=3  [5, 0, 11, 7]
